Manage the IAM users

Usage:
  nexoctl admin user [flags]
  nexoctl admin user [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Create a user
  disable     Disable users (a disabled user cannot sign any request)
  enable      Enable users (a disabled user cannot sign any request)
  info        Show a user
  list        List the users
  policy      Show the policies of a user, direct and inherited from its groups
  remove      Remove users (with their access keys)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for user

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin user [command] --help" for more information about a command.
